**Design Explanation:**
The 7458 chip implements two separate AND-OR logic blocks. The first block (p1y) uses two 3-input AND gates (p1a-p1c and p1d-p1e-p1f) whose outputs are ORed together. The second block (p2y) uses two 2-input AND gates (p2a-p2b and p2c-p2d) whose outputs are ORed together. The design uses intermediate wires for the AND results to make the logic explicit while maintaining the required functionality.

**Implementation:**
```verilog
module TopModule(
  input  p1a, p1b, p1c, p1d, p1e, p1f,
  input  p2a, p2b, p2c, p2d,
  output p1y, p2y
);

  wire and1, and2, and3, and4;

  assign and1 = p1a & p1b & p1c;
  assign and2 = p1d & p1e & p1f;
  assign p1y = and1 | and2;

  assign and3 = p2a & p2b;
  assign and4 = p2c & p2d;
  assign p2y = and3 | and4;

endmodule
```

